<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Massina Jihad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1818</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massina">Massina</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> was a reformist Islamic movement led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seku-amadu">Seku Amadu</a> in the inner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> delta, beginning in 1818. It established the Massina <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a>, a theocratic state in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>. It was one of the West African jihad movements inspired by the example of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>.</p></div>
